{"name":"Pocket Lint","hex":"#b5d5d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pocket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bag stitched to an item of clothing, used for carrying small items.","A person's financial resources."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (something) into a pocket.","To cause a ball to go into one of the pockets of the table; to complete a shot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pocket"},{"term":"lint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clinging fuzzy fluff that clings to fabric or accumulates in one's pockets or navel etc.","A fine material made by scraping cotton or linen cloth; used for dressing wounds."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform a static check on (source code) to detect stylistic or programmatic errors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lint (material)","blocks":[{"text":"Lint is the common name for visible accumulations of textile fibers, hair and other materials, usually found on and around clothing. Certain materials used in the manufacture of clothing, such as cotton, linen, and wool, contain numerous, very short fibers bundled together. During the course of normal wear, these fibers may either detach or be jostled out of the weave of which they are part. This is the reason why heavily used articles, such as shirts and towels, become thin over time and why such particles accumulate in the lint screen of a clothes dryer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Flusensieb_Trockner_02_%28fcm%29.jpg/330px-Flusensieb_Trockner_02_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lint_(material)","wikidata":"Q10815621"},{"title":"Pocket","blocks":[{"text":"A pocket is a small bag- or envelope-shaped compartment that is either sewn into or attached to clothing, designed for carrying small items. Pockets are also found on luggage, backpacks, and similar containers. Historically, the term could also refer to a separate pouch or small bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Jeans_pocket_back.jpg/330px-Jeans_pocket_back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocket","wikidata":"Q321767"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg/500px-Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg/1280px-Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg/500px-Dryer_Lint_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up of dryer lint","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADryer_Lint_Close.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Navel_lint.png/500px-Navel_lint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Navel_lint.png/500px-Navel_lint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Navel lint","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANavel_lint.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Pocket_lint.JPG/500px-Pocket_lint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Pocket_lint.JPG/1280px-Pocket_lint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Pocket_lint.JPG/500px-Pocket_lint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pocket 